  <!-- ===== BEFORE / AFTER ===== -->
  <section class="prog-section ba-section" id="before-after">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Before &amp; after</p>
      <h2 class="prog-section__heading">The same question, before and after the SHARP Method</h2>
      <p class="prog-section__sub">What changes when a student picks the method instead of guessing. An illustrative trigonometry question, not a real student script.</p>

      <div class="ba-question">
        <span class="ba-q-label">Trigonometry &middot; Non-right-angled triangle &middot; 3 marks</span>
        <p>In triangle ABC, AB = 8&nbsp;cm, AC = 6&nbsp;cm and angle BAC = 50&deg;. Find the length of BC.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ba-grid">
        <div class="ba-card ba-card--before">
          <span class="ba-tag ba-tag--before">Before</span>
          <p class="ba-answer">Uses SOH-CAH-TOA: &ldquo;cos&nbsp;50&deg; = BC / 8&rdquo; &rarr; BC = 5.14&nbsp;cm.</p>
          <ul class="ba-notes">
            <li>Assumed a right angle that isn&rsquo;t there</li>
            <li>Wrong tool: SOH-CAH-TOA only works for right-angled triangles</li>
            <li>No valid method, so no method marks</li>
          </ul>
          <span class="ba-mark ba-mark--before">Typically 0 / 3</span>
        </div>

        <div class="ba-card ba-card--after">
          <span class="ba-tag ba-tag--after">After SHARP</span>
          <p class="ba-answer">Right-angle check &rarr; not right-angled; two sides + included angle &rarr; <strong>cosine rule</strong>: BC&sup2; = 8&sup2; + 6&sup2; &minus; 2(8)(6)cos&nbsp;50&deg; &rarr; BC &asymp; 6.19&nbsp;cm.</p>
          <ul class="ba-notes">
            <li><strong>Right-angle check</strong> first: the RULE framework</li>
            <li>Correct tool: two sides &amp; the included angle &rarr; cosine rule</li>
            <li>Full working shown, so every method mark is earned</li>
          </ul>
          <span class="ba-mark ba-mark--after">3 / 3</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="ba-footnote">Checking for a right angle before choosing the method is the <strong>RULE</strong> framework, drilled at the <strong>Hit</strong> step of the SHARP Method.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== INSIDE A LESSON ===== -->
  <section class="prog-section lesson-flow" id="lesson-flow">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inside a lesson</p>
      <h2 class="prog-section__heading">What 90 minutes at <span class="nb">A-Worthy</span> looks like</h2>
      <p class="prog-section__intro">Most parents never see inside a maths tuition lesson. Here&rsquo;s how a typical one runs, from warm-up to homework.</p>

      <ol class="lesson-timeline">
        <li class="lesson-step">
          <span class="lesson-step__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div class="lesson-step__body">
            <span class="lesson-step__time">0 &ndash; 5 min &middot; Retrieval warm-up</span>
            <h3 class="lesson-step__title">Five quick questions on last week</h3>
            <p class="lesson-step__desc">A factorisation, an angle, a ratio problem, a graph sketch and a probability question, all on last week&rsquo;s techniques. Students answer in the chat or on their whiteboards, and anyone who&rsquo;s stuck gets a one-line reminder.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="lesson-step">
          <span class="lesson-step__num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <div class="lesson-step__body">
            <span class="lesson-step__time">5 &ndash; 15 min &middot; Question of the week</span>
            <h3 class="lesson-step__title">Read the question before you solve</h3>
            <p class="lesson-step__desc">We put a real past-paper question on screen and work through the <em>See</em> step together: the command word, what the marks say about the method, and the framework to use. By minute fifteen, every student knows which method the question needs.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="lesson-step">
          <span class="lesson-step__num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <div class="lesson-step__body">
            <span class="lesson-step__time">15 &ndash; 30 min &middot; Framework walkthrough</span>
            <h3 class="lesson-step__title">Name the tool, then use the tool</h3>
            <p class="lesson-step__desc">READ, LABEL, PLOT, DATA, RULE or SHOW, whichever fits the day&rsquo;s topic. Jeremy works a model solution, then writes a flawed version on purpose for students to catch. Because the tool has a name, students can reach for it on exam day without a tutor in the room.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="lesson-step">
          <span class="lesson-step__num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <div class="lesson-step__body">
            <span class="lesson-step__time">30 &ndash; 60 min &middot; Live problem-solving &amp; feedback</span>
            <h3 class="lesson-step__title">Three rounds of feedback per student</h3>
            <p class="lesson-step__desc">Students attempt the question on shared whiteboards. Jeremy moves between their working in real time, flagging missing geometric reasons, sign errors in algebra and the wrong trig formula as they happen. With at most 6 in the group, every student gets feedback at least three times in these thirty minutes.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="lesson-step">
          <span class="lesson-step__num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <div class="lesson-step__body">
            <span class="lesson-step__time">60 &ndash; 75 min &middot; Peer checking</span>
            <h3 class="lesson-step__title">Train the examiner&rsquo;s eye</h3>
            <p class="lesson-step__desc">Students swap solutions and mark each other&rsquo;s working against the mark scheme. Once they see what loses marks in someone else&rsquo;s working, they stop doing it in their own.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="lesson-step">
          <span class="lesson-step__num" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
          <div class="lesson-step__body">
            <span class="lesson-step__time">75 &ndash; 90 min &middot; Exit ticket</span>
            <h3 class="lesson-step__title">No busywork goes home</h3>
            <p class="lesson-step__desc">A two-question exit ticket checks what stuck. Jeremy sets one focused practice piece, usually fifteen minutes&rsquo; work, and sends a worked solution on WhatsApp the next morning. Each piece targets a weakness spotted in that lesson.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="lesson-flow__note">Lessons run weekly on the A-Worthy Whiteboard, and every one is recorded. If your child misses a week, the recording, worksheet and homework reach them within 24 hours.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

